  "scope": "Phase 4-7 of the reusable-contrast-cache milestone: a targeted Discovery V2 implementation (scripts/qbank/contrast_supply.retrieve_targeted_tn_chunks), TDD-covered, replayed over the same 8 prerequisite-ready Development-12 opportunities as development_12_official_discovery_v1.json, for direct V1-vs-V2 comparison. Not a new holdout; Build-12 remains development/training data per the milestone brief.",
  "v1_reference_content_sha256": "1d17394dead1f3323ae3e9c507eac9ef86114a9f9d7fc5aa550868513f072f77",
  "v1_vs_v2_finding": "MIXED, not unambiguously better -- V2's scope restriction is a measured, real precision gain: every V2 candidate is provably drawn from the opportunity's own study unit (V1 was not, per test_targeted_discovery_narrower_than_whole_corpus_baseline, which reproduces at least one off-unit V1 chunk for the same COPD query). Every one of the 8 opportunities now clears a nonzero raw-candidate floor (V1 left 5 of 8 at exactly the same raw count by chance but only 3 opportunities produced any semantic-stage survivor at all). However, a genuinely new, previously undiscovered limitation was found by inspection: because RESPONSE_CLASS_HEADING_FAMILIES selects chunks under TN's generic structural section headings ('Treatment', 'Management', 'Investigations'), most of the top bm25-ranked V2 chunks for RDY-PED-04, RDY-OBGYN-01, RDY-SURG-03 and RDY-SURG-05 carry that same repeated generic subheading with no other identifying metadata, so a specific competing candidate cannot be named from structural metadata alone without reading chunk prose (which this project's copyright policy and discovery methodology both avoid). V1 could sometimes name a specific candidate because Toronto Notes' own 'subheading' field occasionally captures a body-text fragment rather than a clean section title (e.g. 'Purpose: While non-invasive ventilation (NIV) has'), which V2's heading-family filter deliberately excludes because it is not itself a heading-family match by construction, or is simply absent from the measured candidate set at this bm25 rank. This is a genuine metadata-identifiability regression for 4 of 8 opportunities and is reported rather than papered over."
